    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45329" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stentor</span></b> , ŏris,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στέντωρ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Greek warrior in the
				army before Troy</i>, <i>celebrated for the
				strength of his lungs</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 13,
				112</span></i>. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stentŏrĕus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Stentorian</i>, i. e. <i>loud-sounding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vagitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 97</span></i>
			.</div>
